ource.com/401021 Commit-Ready: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja H. Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="401021" owner_email="zachr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/21/401021/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I919dca81cedba210990fd4a574bb98483e7be20a" commit="a0c466a10675df725f83ac1b126627cee47b5600" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: Intel: Skylake: Fix ibs/obs calc for non-integral sampling rates  FW expects sampling rate rounded up to next higher integer value when calculating ibs/obs. For example for 44.1k, it should be rounded up to 45 to calculate ibs/obs.  Signed-off-by: Subhransu S. Prusty &lt;subhransu.s.prusty@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul &lt;vinod.koul@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit f0c8e1d9c4f473dfc771a613b602f1841afe8f8b) Signed-off-by: Vijay G Krishna &lt;vijay.g.krishna@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56175 TEST=Play mp3 file from local storage TEST=Connect 4K monitor via USB-C HDMI TEST=Observe audio quality from monitor output  Change-Id: I919dca81cedba210990fd4a574bb98483e7be20a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399599 Commit-Ready: Vijay G Krishna &lt;vijay.g.krishna@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Casey G Bowman &lt;casey.g.bowman@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vedang Patel &lt;vedang.patel@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399599" owner_email="vijay.g.krishna@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/99/399599/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If5090c60e4f1bddc3256e3350231b5b82f702eb6" commit="531ad9d6484631ce3b1e7b4b28cf368fb86adddc" commit_message="FROMLIST: ASoC: Intel: Skylake: Use DPIB to update position for Playback stream  DPIB is read currently from a buffer position in memory (indicated by the registers DPIB[U|L]BASE).Driver reads the position buffer on BDL completion interrupts to report the DMA position. But the BDL completion interrupt only indicates the last DMA transfer of the buffer is completed at the Intel HD Audio subsystem boundary. The periodic DMA Position-in-Buffer writes may be scheduled at the same time or later than the MSI and does not guarantee to reflect the position of the last buffer that was transferred.  Whereas DPIB register in HDA space(vendor specific register indicated by SDxDPIB) reflects the actual data that is transferred. Hence update the position based on DPIB for playback.  Signed-off-by: Dharageswari R &lt;dharageswari.r@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Jeeja KP &lt;jeeja.kp@intel.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9363637/) Signed-off-by: Vijay G Krishna &lt;vijay.g.krishna@intel.com&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:56175, chrome-os-partner:55655 TEST=Play mp3 file from local storage TEST=Connect 4K monitor via USB-C HDMI TEST=Observe audio quality from monitor output  Change-Id: If5090c60e4f1bddc3256e3350231b5b82f702eb6 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/399600 Commit-Ready: Vijay G Krishna &lt;vijay.g.krishna@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Casey G Bowman &lt;casey.g.bowman@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Vedang Patel &lt;vedang.patel@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="399600" owner_email="vijay.g.krishna@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/00/399600/1" remote="cros" 